This is a technical article for the visa articles of Wiki. The article presents visa conditions for different countries.

#section-h::Template:Transcluded sections for the visa articles|Section

==Abkhazia. Visa==
* Tourists from all countries (except Georgia) can visit Abkhazia for a period not exceeding 24 hours as part of an organized tourist group.

==Afghanistan. eVisa==
* A visa is not required for individuals born in Afghanistan or for those who can provide proof that one of their parents is an Afghan national or was born in Afghanistan.<ref>{{Cite web |title=E-Afghans Visa Portal - Your Digital Gateway to Travel |url=https://eafghans.com/ |access-date=2026-03-25 |website=eafghans.com |language=en}}</ref>
* e-Visa : Visitors must arrive at Kabul International (KBL).

==Algeria. VOA==
* Persons may be denied entry if entering with a passport containing visas or stamps issued by Israel.
* Visitors on tours organized to some southern regions by an approved travel agency may obtain a visa on arrival for up to 30 days.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://embassyofalgeria.ie/exceptional-measures-for-tourists-traveling-to-southern-algeria/ | title=Exceptional measures for tourists traveling to southern Algeria | publisher=Algerian Embassy in Ireland}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://againstthecompass.com/en/travel-algeria/ | title=How to travel to Algeria | date=20 February 2026}}</ref>

==Angola. VOA==
* 30 days per trip, but no more than 90 days within any 1 calendar year for tourism purposes only.<ref>[https://allafrica.com/stories/201803280299.html Angola: Migration Service to Speed Up Visa Exemption Procedure]</ref>
* Visitors must have a return/onward ticket and a hotel reservation confirmation.<ref>{{Timatic Visa Policy | accessdate=2 November 2022}}</ref>
* An [[International Certificate of Vaccination]] is required.

==Benin. eVisa==
* Must have an international vaccination certificate.
* Three types of electronic visa are offered: the e-Visa valid for 30 days for a single entry (50 EUR), the e-Visa valid for 30 days for several (multiple) entries (75 EUR), and the e-Visa valid for 90 days to make several (multiple) entries (100 EUR).<ref>{{cite web |url=https://evisa.bj/articles/costs-of-entry-visas-to-benin/8c948600-ca08-443e-bac9-33aae6583b54 |title=Costs of entry visas to Benin}}</ref>

==Bhutan. SDF==
* The [[Visa policy of Bhutan#Sustainable Development Fee|Sustainable Development Fee]] (SDF) of 200 [[USD]] per person, per night for almost all visitors to Bhutan. Additionally, if payment is made in US dollars from September 1, 2023 to August 31, 2027, the SDF is 100 USD.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://immi.gov.bt/faq/ | title=Frequently Asked Questions - Bhutan Immigration Services Portal}}</ref>

==Cape Verde. TSA==
* Must register online at least five days prior to arrival.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.ease.gov.cv | title=Cape Verde EASE}}</ref>
* Visitors must pay the Airport Security Fee (TSA) before visiting. The cost is 3,400 CVE (approx. 31 [[EUR]]) and can be paid via the online platform (EASE).

==Cape Verde. VOA==
* Visa on arrival may applied for via the online platform (EASE) and issued at international airports in [[Sal, Cape Verde (municipality)|Sal]], [[Boa Vista, Cape Verde (municipality)|Boa Vista]], [[São Vicente, Cape Verde|São Vicente]] or [[Santiago, Cape Verde|Santiago]]. Visa fee is approximately 25–30 EUR.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.capeverdeislands.org/visa/ | title=Cape Verde visa information}}</ref>
* Visitors must pay the Airport Security Fee (TSA) before visiting. The cost is 3,400 CVE (approx. 31 [[EUR]]) and can be paid via the online platform (EASE).

==China. Transit==
* 240-hour (10-day) visa-free transit to a third country or region (including [[Hong Kong]], [[Macau]] or [[Taiwan]]) using any mode of transport. Must have a confirmed onward ticket/itinerary, and enter through 1 of 64 [[Visa policy of mainland China#visa-free transit|approved ports]].
** During which, may freely travel within  [[Visa policy of mainland China#Visa-free transit|the 24 provinces permitted for visa-free transit]] and engage in tourism, business, and visits.<ref name="NIA-VFT">{{cite web |title=Visa-Free Transit Policies |website=National Immigration Administration |date=2025-07-04 |url=https://en.nia.gov.cn/n147418/n147463/c183412/content.html |language=en |access-date=2025-12-24 |url-status=live}}</ref>

* 24-hour visa-free transit to a third country or region (including Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan), is available at [[Visa policy of mainland China#24-hour_Transit_Without_a_Visa|most international airports]], without leaving the airport.<ref name="NIA-VFT" />
** Travellers who need to leave the airport may obtain a temporary entry permit from [[National Immigration Administration|immigration]].<ref name="NIA-VFT" />

* 5-day port visa (Visa on Arrival) for [[Shenzhen]] if arriving at [[Visa policy of mainland China|designated ports of entry]] from Hong Kong by land or sea, for stays within Shenzhen.
* 3-day port visa (Visa on Arrival) if arriving in [[Zhuhai]] or [[Xiamen]] at [[Visa policy of mainland China|designated ports of entry]], for stays within the respective city.

* 15-day visa-free entry for cruise ship passengers in tour groups, if arriving at any cruise port along China's coastline, including but not limited to [[Tianjin]]; [[Dalian]]; [[Shanghai]]; [[Lianyungang]]; [[Wenzhou]]; [[Zhoushan]]; [[Xiamen]]; [[Qingdao]]; [[Guangzhou]]; [[Shenzhen]]; [[Beihai]]; [[Haikou]]; [[Sanya]]. May further travel inland to all regions of coastal provinces (and equivalents) and Beijing.<ref>{{cite web |title=Visa-Free Entry Policy for Foreign Tourist Groups Traveling by Cruise Ships Effective on May 15 |website=National Immigration Administration |date=2024-05-17 |url=https://en.nia.gov.cn/n147413/c160799/content.html |language=en |access-date=2025-12-24 |url-status=live}}</ref>

* May apply for a port visa (Visa on Arrival) if travelling for an urgent, qualified reason. Prior clearance for port visa is highly recommended or may be denied boarding by airlines.<ref>{{cite web
 |title=FAQs About Port Visas and Other Related Issues
 |url=https://en.nia.gov.cn/n147418/n147463/c156102/content.html
 |website=National Immigration Administration
 |date=2024-02-29
 |access-date=2025-12-25
 |language=en
}}</ref>

==Christmas Island and Cocos (Keeling) Islands==
* 90 days; Passports and visas are not required when travelling from the Australian mainland. However, photographic identification must be produced for clearance through Customs and Immigration. Normal Australian Customs and Immigration procedures apply when entry is made from outside Australia.

==Ethiopia. eVisa/VOA==
* Visa on arrival is obtainable only at [[Addis Ababa Bole International Airport]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Ethiopia visa on arrival|publisher=Main Department for Immigration and Nationality Affairs, Ethiopia|url=https://www.evisa.gov.et/#/visaonarrival|access-date=24 November 2018}}</ref>
* e-Visa holders must arrive via [[Addis Ababa Bole International Airport]].
* e-Visa is available for 30 or 90 days.<ref>{{cite web|title=Ethiopia electronic visa|publisher=Main Department for Immigration and Nationality Affairs, Ethiopia|url=https://www.evisa.gov.et|access-date=24 November 2018}}</ref>

==Falkland Islands. Visitor permit==
* A visitor permit is normally issued as a stamp in the passport on arrival, The maximum validity period is 1 month.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.gov.fk/customs/visitor-permit/ |title=Visitor Permit}}</ref>

==Galápagos. Pre-registration==
* 60 days; Visitors must pre-register to receive a 20 USD Transit Control Card (TCT).<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.gobiernogalapagos.gob.ec/para-ingresar-a-la-provincia-de-galapagos/ | title=Para ingresar a la provincia de Galapagos}}</ref>

==Guyana. eVisa==
* An eVisa(Approval letter) can only be obtained after contacting the Department of Immigration and Citizenship by phone. 
* Payment is done upon arrival.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.embassyofguyana.be/services.php?sid=34 | title=Embassy of Guyana in Belgium - eVisa instructions}}</ref>

