==Liberia. eVisa==
*The Liberia Visa on Arrival (VoA) allows travelers to obtain a Visa upon arrival in Liberia by plane. Travelers must pre-apply for the visa online.

==Libya. eVisa==
* Independent travel is not permitted, and visitors must organize their visit through a tour guide. A tourist police escort is required at all times.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://againstthecompass.com/en/travel-libya/#comments | title=Libya eVisa information}}</ref>
* An eVisa will not be granted without a sponsor or tour agency.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.saigatours.com/article/How-to-apply-for-the-Libyan-evisa | title=How to Apply for the Libya eVisa}}</ref>
* A security letter issued by the Libyan Immigration Authorities may also be required.<ref>{{Timatic Visa Policy|country=LY|access-date=16 May 2026}}</ref>
* Holders of passports containing an Israeli stamp or visa will be refused entry in Libya.

==Malaysia. MDAC==
* The electronic Malaysia Digital Arrival Card must be submitted within three days before the date of arrival in Malaysia.<ref>{{cite web | title=Malaysia Digital Arrival Card | url=https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main}}</ref>

==Myanmar. eVisa==
* e-Visa holders must arrive via [[Yangon International Airport|Yangon]], [[Naypyidaw Airport|Nay Pyi Taw]] or [[Mandalay International Airport|Mandalay]] airports or via land border crossings with [[Thailand]] — [[Tachileik]], [[Myawaddy]] and [[Kawthaung]] or [[India]] — [[Rih Khaw Dar]] and [[Tamu, Myanmar|Tamu]].
* e-Visa available for both tourism or business purposes.

==Namibia. Visa on arrival==
* Visa on arrival is available at the following locations:
** [[Hosea Kutako International Airport]]
** [[Impalila Island]]
** [[Katima Mulilo]]
** [[Ngoma, Namibia|Ngoma]]
** Trans Kalahari ([[Buitepos]])
** [[Walvis Bay Airport]]

==Norfolk Island. Travel==
* 30 days; Visa is issued upon arrival for a visit of up to max stay of 120 days, for holders of a multiple entry Electronic Travel authority (ETA) issued by Australia, valid 30 days beyond the period of intended stay in Norfolk Island.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.legislation.gov.au/C2015Q00153/latest/text | title=Norfolk Island Immigration Act 1980 | publisher=
Federal Register of Legislation | quote=PART 6 — GENERAL : Transitional provisions}}</ref>
* From 1 July 2016 all movement between Norfolk Island and Australian mainland are considered as domestic movement, however all passenger are still required to carry passports or, for Australian citizens, some type of photographic identification and pass Customs and Immigration. Normal Australian Customs and Immigration procedures apply when entry is made from outside Australia. Passenger not carrying their passports are not eligible to purchase duty-free goods on Norfolk Island.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.nirc.gov.au/Your-council/Norfolk-Island-Legislation | title=Legislation Applied to Norfolk Island | publisher=Norfolk Island Regional Council}}</ref>

==Pakistan. Online Visa/1==
* Online Visa eligible.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://visa.nadra.gov.pk/tourist-visa/ | title=Tourist Visa}}</ref>
* Issued in 7-10 business days.

==Pakistan. Online Visa/2==
* Online Visa eligible.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://visa.nadra.gov.pk/tourist-visa/ | title=Tourist Visa}}</ref>
* Issued in 7-10 business days.

==Papua New Guinea. eVisa==
* Visitors may apply for a visa online under the "Tourist - Own Itinerary" category.

==Seychelles. SEBS==
* Application can be submitted up to 30 days before travel.
* Visitors must upload a reservation confirmation(s) for each visitor's location of stay in Seychelles.
* Yellow fever vaccination certificate is required if coming from endemic countries.
* Payment of the fee (EUR 10) by credit or debit card.
* Valid for one journey only and it expires once exit the country.

==Somalia. eTAS==
* All visitors must have an approved Electronic Visa (eTAS) before the start of their journey.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://visasnews.com/en/somalia-modernizes-its-electronic-visa-service/ | title=New visa policy of Somalia}}</ref>

==Somalia. VOA==
* All visitors must have an approved Electronic Visa (eTAS) before the start of their journey.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://visasnews.com/en/somalia-modernizes-its-electronic-visa-service/ | title=New visa policy of Somalia}}</ref>

==Somalia. VOA/3==

* Available at [[Berbera]], [[Borama]], [[Burao]], [[Erigavo]] and [[Hargeisa]] airports.{{Citation needed|date=November 2022}} 
* 30 days, available at [[Bosaso Airport]], [[Galcaio Airport]] and [[Mogadishu Airport]].{{Citation needed|date=November 2022}}

==South Ossetia. Visa==
* To enter South Ossetia, visitors must have a multiple-entry visa for [[Russia]] and register their stay with the Migration Service of the Ministry of Internal Affairs within 3 days.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.mfa-rso.su/taxonomy/term/13 | title=Порядок въезда на территорию Республики Южная Осетия для иностранных граждан}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://mfa.rsogov.org/node/1398 | title=Порядок въезда на территорию Республики Южная Осетия для иностранных граждан}}</ref>

==South Sudan. eVisa==
* Obtainable online 30 days single entry for 100 USD, 90 days multiple entry for 200 USD and 180 days multiple entry for 350 USD.
* Printed visa authorization must be presented at the time of travel.

==Sri Lanka. ETA==
* Sri Lanka introduced an ETA valid for 30 days.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://eta.gov.lk/ | title=Sri Lanka ETA}}</ref>

==Sri Lanka. eVisa==
* Sri Lanka introduced an ETA valid for 30 days.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://eta.gov.lk/ | title=Sri Lanka ETA}}</ref>

==Sri Lanka. Visa in advance==
* Below are the documents required:
** Police Clearance report
** If the applicant is coming from another country after staying for more than 6 months, are required to provide Police clearance from that country and copy of the Visa
** Certificate from a Sri Lankan guarantor & a photocopy of the guarantors NIC
** Affidavit from a Sri Lankan JP (Justice of Peace) or a Lawyer
** Accommodation information (Place of stay)

==Suriname. Information==
* An entrance fee of [[USD]] 50 or EUR 50 must be paid online prior to arrival.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://suriname.vfsevisa.com/suriname/online/home/visa-fees | title=Entry-fee}}</ref>
* Multiple entry e-Visa is also available.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://suriname.vfsevisa.com/suriname/online/home/who-can-apply-for-eVisa | title=Suriname eVisa &#124; VFS Global &#124; Official partner of the Government of Suriname}}</ref>

==Transnistria. Migration card==
* Visitors must complete and obtain a temporary migration card at the border checkpoint. The maximum period of stay is 45 days, and it can be extended multiple times through this card.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://ulpmr.ru/ul/show/i6OdSKF4TWgCw01WMzY8Ww16zDnXsDVwjNPY= |title=On the legal status of foreign citizens and stateless persons in the Transnistria |date=2017-05-31 |access-date=2023-12-30 |website=ulpmr.ru}}</ref>

==Turkmenistan. Visa==
* 10-day visa on arrival if holding a letter of invitation provided by a company registered in Turkmenistan with a prior approval from the [[Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Turkmenistan)|Foreign Ministry]]. Visitors can apply to extend their stay for an additional 10 days.<ref>{{cite web | title=TÜRKMENISTANYŇ DÖWLET MIGRASIÝA GULLUGY | url=https://migration.gov.tm/services/wiza-we-is-rugsatnamasy-16847397661914537 | access-date=2025-01-10 | website=migration.gov.tm}}</ref>
* When transiting between two non-bordering countries, visitors can obtain a Turkmenistan transit visa for a five-day stay. This must be applied for in advance at the Turkmenistan Embassy. Visitors must also submit copies of the visas for the country of entry into Turkmenistan and the country of departure from Turkmenistan. Visa fee is 20 USD.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://migration.gov.tm/services/wiza-we-is-rugsatnamasy-16847397661914537 | title=Turkmenistan Visa}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://uk.tmembassy.gov.tm/en/consular-services/visa-info | title=Visa info}}</ref>

==Turkmenistan. Transit Visa==
* When transiting between two non-bordering countries, visitors can obtain a Turkmenistan transit visa for a five-day stay. This must be applied for in advance at the Turkmenistan Embassy. Visitors must also submit copies of the visas for the country of entry into Turkmenistan and the country of departure from Turkmenistan. Visa fee is 20 USD.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://migration.gov.tm/services/wiza-we-is-rugsatnamasy-16847397661914537 | title=Turkmenistan Visa}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://uk.tmembassy.gov.tm/en/consular-services/visa-info | title=Visa info}}</ref>

==United States. ESTA==
* [[Electronic System for Travel Authorization|ESTA]] is valid for 2 years from the date of issuance.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://help.cbp.gov/s/article/Article-1072?language=en_US | title=CBP Customer Service | publisher=Help.cbp.gov | date= | accessdate=2022-03-06}}</ref>
* ESTA is also required when entering the country by cruise ship or land.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.cbp.gov/newsroom/national-media-release/cbp-expands-esta-requirements-visa-waiver-program-travelers | title=Entry into the United States by land, sea, or air}}</ref>
* A [[Form I-94]] is required for entry into the United States by land. It carries a $30 fee and can be obtained either online or upon arrival.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://i94.cbp.dhs.gov/home |title=I-94/I-95 Website |publisher=U.S. Customs and Border Protection |location=Washington, D.C.}}</ref>
* Visa required for nationals of VWP countries who have travelled or been present in Iran, Iraq, Libya, North Korea, Somalia, Sudan, Syria or Yemen at any time on or after 1 March 2011 or Cuba at any time on or after 12 January 2021, or nationals of VWP countries who are also nationals of Iran, Iraq, North Korea, Sudan or Syria. Exceptions apply if the travel was in military or diplomatic service of the VWP country.

==Uzbekistan. Transit==
* 5-day visa-free transit at the international airports if holding a confirmed onward ticket for a flight to a third country.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.lex.uz/docs/3810645|title=ПОСТАНОВЛЕНИЕ ПРЕЗИДЕНТА РЕСПУБЛИКИ УЗБЕКИСТАН О ДАЛЬНЕЙШИХ МЕРАХ ПО ОПТИМИЗАЦИИ ПОРЯДКА ВЪЕЗДА ИНОСТРАННЫХ ГРАЖДАН В РЕСПУБЛИКУ УЗБЕКИСТАН|date=4 July 2018|website=lex.uz|access-date=15 July 2018}}</ref>

==Yemen. eVisa/1==
* Yemen introduced an e-Visa system for visitors who meet certain eligibility requirements (group travel of 10 or more people, business trips, and transit etc.).<ref>{{cite web | url=https://yemenevisa.org/visas | title=Yemen eVisa}}</ref>

==Yemen. eVisa/2==
* Separately, Yemen introduced an e-Visa system for visitors who meet certain eligibility requirements (group travel of 10 or more people, business trips, and transit etc.).<ref>{{cite web | url=https://yemenevisa.org/visas | title=Yemen eVisa}}</ref>

